A||||4||Uaana||Auto Shifting probs||||1||
Z||000000||Uaana||01-18-2001||03:27 AM||||Noticed this a couple of times lately.<BR>When I am engaged in hard cornering my auto tranny likes to ?slip into neutral? <BR>Basically if I take a corner too hard the engine will wind out like it's in neutral unless I get off the gas and let her straigten out.<BR>Any suggestions?<BR>Just checked the fluid level and it's full.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||01-19-2001||08:38 AM||||Bump. Anyone???<BR>Guess next time I'll ask about speaker installs....||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||01-19-2001||09:06 AM||||crappy filter maybe... under high lateral g's the filter may not be totally submerged and the only the clogged part of the filter is getting any fluid.. a filter kit is like $12 from NAPA and it takes about an hour to do.. 5minutes to jack it up, 35minutes to let all the fluid drain into a recycling jug so none drips RIGHT into your eye, 5 minutes to change the filter, 10min to fight with the gasket and 5 to let the car down. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||01-19-2001||10:04 AM||||Uaana,<P>Did you check the tranny fluid with the motor warmed up and running?  <BR>(Sorry if this is a stupid question.)<BR>If not, start the engine, and shift slowly through all the gears, ending up in park. This should purge all the air from the hydraulics. Then check the fluid with the engine running. <P>It really does sound like the pump is sucking wind.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||01-19-2001||02:47 PM||||This is not uncommon on 125C's. Check the fluid by averaging the front and back of the dip stick and run it at the max level. This assumes the filter it not clogged.<P>Certainly, something else can be wrong, but those are common symptoms. I noticed it in parking lots on hard fast turns.||||reg||1
